export const title = "Device Audio Output";
export const html = "<h1>Device Audio Output</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>AI Bridge supports audio output, and you can register event actions per channel, integrate with a VMS, or apply it to a variety of other scenarios.</p>\n<p>The AI Bridge audio line output is mono, but the signal is duplicated to output on 2 channels (stereo).</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Prerequisites</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">You need an audio output device prepared and hardware-connected to the unit.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">On 4-channel units, connect an amplified active speaker to the port labeled <strong>AUDIO LINE OUT</strong>. On 8-channel units, connect it to the <strong>AUDIO LINE OUT</strong> port on the rear panel.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2a2f3a,#12151c);border-radius:10px;padding:22px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-around;color:#cfd6e6;font-size:11px;text-align:center;\">\n  <div>&#128266;<br>POWER</div>\n  <div style=\"color:#f0c26b;\">&#9679;<br>AUDIO LINE IN</div>\n  <div style=\"color:#7fbf95;\">&#9679;<br>AUDIO LINE OUT</div>\n  <div>&#9645;<br>MICRO SD</div>\n  <div>&#9645;<br>USB</div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>4-channel unit rear panel &mdash; connect an amplified active speaker to AUDIO LINE OUT</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>In <strong>Audio</strong> settings, confirm that the setting below is checked for the channel you want to use, and set its priority.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Audio Input</th><th>Camera Speaker</th><th>Device Speaker</th><th>Priority</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CH1</td><td>Camera - 1</td><td><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled></td><td><select disabled><option>Normal</option></select></td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Audio settings &mdash; enable Device Speaker for the channel and set its priority</figcaption>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If speaker output happens on multiple channels at the same time, the audio from the channel with the higher priority is what plays.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Configuring the Action</h2>\n<p>Select <strong>Audio Output</strong> as the action type on the action settings screen to configure device speaker output.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>Audio Output</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to Audio Output reveals the related settings below it. Check the <strong>Device Audio Output</strong> checkbox.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:170px 1fr;\">\n    <span>&#9432; Device Audio Output</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    <span>&#9432; Priority</span><select disabled><option>Normal</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Select the sound source to play on the device. New sound files can be added from the <strong>New</strong> tab. Supported formats are mp3 and wav.</p>\n<p>From the <strong>Recently Added</strong> tab, choose a sound already registered in the list to output on the device.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;gap:16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:10px;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span style=\"padding-bottom:6px;\">New</span><span style=\"padding-bottom:6px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--blue);color:var(--blue);font-weight:700;\">Recently Added</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:8px 4px;\">\n    <span>&#9679; Intrusion Warning</span>\n    <span style=\"font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Edit &nbsp; Delete</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Audio File (mp3/wav) &mdash; New / Recently Added</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">&#8251; Uploaded files must be 5MB or smaller. The audio file's bitrate and channel count don't matter.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Click the Test button to confirm the currently selected sound plays correctly on the device.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:260px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Audio Test</span> &nbsp; <span class=\"btn small primary\">Test</span></div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">If the test volume seems low, adjust it from the Audio Volume tab.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">Note. If the volume is still too low at maximum, check the volume on the connected speaker itself.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. For louder output, connect an amplified active speaker.</p>";
